@program gtk3-text-input-test
@compositor gnome
@conf hime-edit-display=2
@conf hime-on-the-spot-key=1
# As wl-im-repeat.keys, through GNOME's IBus (hime-ibus), except the end:
# GNOME repeats held keys itself, and passes no repeats of a key on to the
# application unless it saw the press; hime-ibus passes each one on, so
# BackSpace goes on deleting the text (here both characters).
# HIME repeats a held key it handles; once the keys typed are gone, the
# application gets the key, once: it would only repeat it after its own
# delay, and gets the release before that.
a <space> a <space> b c d @check @hold <bs>
